                'and Data Protection (General) Regulations, 2021. The personal data collected as detailed will, '
                'therefore, be processed in line with the relevant Data Protection Policies, Laws and Regulations in '
                'the way(s) and purpose(s) detailed in this Consent Form. Pursuant to the Data Protection (General) '
                'Regulations, 2021. Kisii University, in its capacity as a data controller and processor under the '
                'Data Protection Act, 2019, must obtain your voluntary, explicit, affirmative, and informed consent '
                'before it can collect or process any personal data for a lawful basis, including, but not limited to, '
                'employment, admission and enrollment, study, internship, online education, online activities etc. The '
                'University collects the following personal data for responsible, and strictly, official purposes: '
                'Identification details: Name, National Identification Card/ Passport Number, Birth Certificate '
                'Number, Images (photographs/videos). Contact details: Phone number, Post Office Box, Email address '
                'Academic qualifications details: Through your academic certificates Geographical location details The '
                'University collects and processes the above-mentioned personal data for the following purposes: '
                'Confirming the identity of a student for security purposes and controlled access to University '
                'services. Managing student processes including admission processing, teaching and research, '
                'examinations handling and co-curricular activities. Generating statistics and reports that will be '
                'used for planning and decision-making as well as guiding policy development and implementation. '
                'Reporting to affiliated government agencies and regulatory bodies such as the Ministry of Education, '
                'the Commission for University Education (CUE), the Kenya National Bureau of Statistics (KNBS), the '
                'Kenya Universities & Colleges Central Placement Services (KUCCPS), the Higher Education Loans Board '
                '(HELB) among others. All personal data provided to Kisii University, and all the further data '
                'provided to allow the processing of your application to Kisii University academic courses, and '
                'thereof aimed at the performance of the related services to be provided to you, will be processed and '
                'handled by the University in accordance with its policies and with the aforementioned Law, and with '
                'the principles of fairness, lawfulness, transparency, purpose limitation, accuracy, storage '
                'limitation, integrity and confidentiality and accountability, as well as the utmost protection of '
                'your privacy; sensitive data processing will only take place in relation to data regarding your '
                'sensitive data as listed below. Personal data revealing race, health status, ethnic social origin, '
                'conscience, belief, genetic data, biometric data, property details, marital status, family details '
                'including names of your children, parents, spouse or spouses, sex or sexual orientation, criminal '
                'convictions and offences (collectively “Sensitive Data”) may be requested by Kisii University. With '
                'the exception of criminal convictions, you are not obligated to provide Sensitive Data and do so on a '
                'voluntary basis. If Sensitive Data is provided to Kisii University, your signature shall be consent '
                'to the University to process Sensitive Data for the purposes described in this Consent and in '
                'accordance with the Data Protection Act, 2019 and Data Protection (General) Regulations, 2021. '
                'Sensitive Data may be processed by Kisii University for the following purposes and subject to '
                'appropriate safeguards: Recruitment of you to participate in Kisii University programs; Performance '
                'of a contract with you and/or the Partner Institution defined below, or in order to take action on '
                'your request to the University prior to entering into the contract; Compliance with a legal '
                'obligation to which Kisii University is subject; Protection of your vital interests or those of '
                'another person; Performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of '
                'official authority vested in Kisii University, including the enforcement of the University academic '
                'policies and procedures, and the Student Code of Conduct; Carrying out obligations and specific '
                'rights in the field of employment, social security or a collective bargaining agreement; The exercise '
                'or defense of legal claims; Preventive or occupational medicine, the assessment of your capacity as a '
                'student, or medical diagnosis of the health or treatment, or management of health and services for '
                'you; Protection of public health and prevention of disease; Archiving purposes in the public '
                'interest, scientific or historical research purposes, or statistical purposes. Notwithstanding '
                'anything to the contrary herein, Kisii University may process personal data without the data '
                'subject’s consent under certain other lawful bases, including when processing is necessary for the '
                'performance of a contract to which a data subject is a party; when processing is necessary for '
                'compliance with a legal obligation to which Kisii University is subject; or when processing is '
                'necessary to protect vital interests, such as the life of a data subject. Personal data will be '
                'handled and processed only by the persons who are responsible for the necessary activities for the '
                'purpose above. Refusal of consent may make it impossible for Kisii University to carry out its '
                'necessary activities for the purpose above, and may hamper the University’s ability to provide '
                'requested [educational services] [employment] [participation in a research] [other] to you. You will '
                'be able to exercise any and all other rights, as applicable, foreseen by the Data Protection Act and '
                'the Regulations thereto namely right of access, right to rectification, right to erasure or “to be '
                'forgotten”, right to restriction of processing, right to data portability and the right to object. '
                'You have the right to withdraw your consent to the collection and processing of personal data. If you '
                'would like to withdraw consent, please contact the Data Protection Officer at '
                'dpo@kisiiuniversity.ac.ke . mode_comment close Kisii University Support close Hi Welcome to Kisii '
